INFO     rag_service.services.generation_service:generation_service.py:427 {"event": "rag_query_trace", "query": "What is the planned sample size and statistical power?", "retrieval_query": null, "system_prompt_version": "440b2406", "retrieved_chunks": [{"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 12, "section": "Sample Size", "score": 0.9383503, "scores": null, "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 66, "section": "9.1 Determination of Sample Size", "score": null, "scores": [0.9328214, 0.03676947], "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 29, "section": "3.2 Planned Number of Patients", "score": 0.07935289, "scores": null, "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 67, "section": "9.6.1 General Considerations", "score": 0.021698097, "scores": null, "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 14, "section": "Data Analyses", "score": 0.02132808, "scores": null, "had_context": true}], "context_char_count": 5531, "response": "Source: Protocol Ulcerative Colitis\n\nThe planned enrollment is 90 patients with active ulcerative colitis, competitively enrolled across approximately 25\u201330 investigational sites globally and randomized equally among three arms: two TJ301 dose levels and placebo.\n[Section 3.2 Planned Number of Patients \u00b7 p.29]\n\nThe statistical sample size is 72 evaluable patients (24 per treatment/placebo arm). This provides 83% power to detect a one-sided trend at p<0.05 for a 30% Week 12 remission-rate difference between placebo and 600 mg Q2W (10% versus 40%), using Pearson\u2019s chi-square test without continuity correction.\n[Section 9.1 Determination of Sample Size \u00b7 p.66]\n\nThe trial has 70% power for a one-sided p<0.05 statistically significant result if the Week 12 remission-rate difference between placebo and the combined 300 mg Q2W plus 600 mg Q2W treatment groups is 20% (10% versus 30%). Approximately 20% dropout was anticipated, so 90 patients will be enrolled.\n[Section 9.1 Determination of Sample Size \u00b7 p.66]", "sources": [{"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 29, "section": "3.2 Planned Number of Patients", "exactText": "In total, 90 patients with active UC at approximately 25-30 investigational sites globally will be enrolled competitively and randomised equally into three arms with TJ301 (two dose levels) or placebo.", "bboxes": [[72.0, 653.5439829101564, 534.48, 612.8949752178487]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 66, "section": "9.1 Determination of Sample Size", "exactText": "A sample size of N=72 (n=24 per treatment/placebo arm) patients is expected to achieve a power of 83 % of detecting a trend (p< 0.05, one-sided) if the true remission rate difference (at Week 12) between the placebo and highest dose groups (600 mg Q2W) is 30% (10% for the placebo and 40% for the highest dose) using Pearson's chi-square test without continuity correction. The trial also has 70 % power to reach a statistical ly significant result (p<0.05, one-sided) in case the remission rate difference between placebo and treatment (300 mg Q2W and 600 mg Q2W combined together) is 20% (10% vs 30%). Considering the dropout rate of approximately 20 %, a total of 90 patients will be enrolled competitively.", "bboxes": [[72.00000000000006, 583.8239829101564, 554.16, 467.33497521784864], [72.0, 671.7839829101564, 552.4800000000001, 600.7749752178487]], "relevance": "high"}], "timing": {"response_cache_hit": false, "semantic_cache_hit": false, "chunks_compressed": true, "condense_ms": 0.01837499439716339, "query_condensed": false, "embedding_ms": 720.2267092652619, "embedding_cache_hit": false, "retrieval": {"chunk_cache_hit": false, "confidence_filter_applied": true, "confidence_filter_threshold": 0.04, "confidence_filter_bm25_threshold": null, "confidence_filter_input_count": 45, "confidence_filter_kept_count": 45, "confidence_filter_dropped_coun