INFO     rag_service.services.generation_service:generation_service.py:427 {"event": "rag_query_trace", "query": "What fields should the eCRF include based on this protocol?", "retrieval_query": null, "system_prompt_version": "440b2406", "retrieved_chunks": [{"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 75, "section": "12.2 Deviations from the Protocol", "score": 0.48947302, "scores": null, "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 71, "section": "10.2 Electronic Case Record Form", "score": null, "scores": [0.36692992, 0.022542967], "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 63, "section": "8.5.2 Collection, Recording and Reporting of Serious Adverse Events SAE Reporting by the Investigator", "score": null, "scores": [0.09073549, 0.053899154], "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 58, "section": "8.2.2 Recording of Adverse Events", "score": 0.026056303, "scores": null, "had_context": true}], "context_char_count": 7020, "response": "Source: Protocol Ulcerative Colitis\n\nThe protocol specifies the following e-CRF fields for each patient\u2019s Adverse Event Log:\n\n1. Adverse event\n[Section 8.2.2 Recording of Adverse Events \u00b7 p.58]\n\n2. Date of onset (time can be recorded, if applicable)\n[Section 8.2.2 Recording of Adverse Events \u00b7 p.58]\n\n3. Intensity\n[Section 8.2.2 Recording of Adverse Events \u00b7 p.58]\n\n4. Causal relationship to IMP\n[Section 8.2.2 Recording of Adverse Events \u00b7 p.58]\n\n5. Action taken to IMP\n[Section 8.2.2 Recording of Adverse Events \u00b7 p.58]\n\n6. Other action taken\n[Section 8.2.2 Recording of Adverse Events \u00b7 p.58]\n\n7. Date and time of outcome\n[Section 8.2.2 Recording of Adverse Events \u00b7 p.58]\n\n8. Outcome\n[Section 8.2.2 Recording of Adverse Events \u00b7 p.58]\n\n9. Seriousness\n[Section 8.2.2 Recording of Adverse Events \u00b7 p.58]\n\nFor SAE reporting, the protocol also identifies the Demographics, Medical History Log, and Concomitant Medication Log as mandatory, along with the Adverse Event Log; however, I don't have this information regarding the individual fields required within those additional logs.\n[Section 8.5.2 Collection, Recording and Reporting of Serious Adverse Events SAE Reporting by the Investigator \u00b7 p.63]\n\nThe e-CRF must also support electronic correction of errors, with an audit trail that records the date and time of each correction and the name of the person making it.\n[Section 10.2 Electronic Case Record Form \u00b7 p.71]", "sources": [{"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 58, "section": "8.2.2 Recording of Adverse Events", "exactText": "The Investigator must record all adverse events in the Adverse Event Log provided in each patient's e-CRF with information about:\n- Adverse event\n- Date of onset (time can be recorded, if applicable)\n- Intensity\n- Causal relationship to IMP\n- Action taken to IMP\n- Other action taken\n- Date and time of outcome\n- Outcome\n- Seriousness", "bboxes": [[72.00000000000011, 188.78398291015662, 511.32, 163.25497521784894]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 63, "section": "8.5.2 Collection, Recording and Reporting of Serious Adverse Events SAE Reporting by the Investigator", "exactText": "Completion of the Demographics, Adverse Event Log, Medical History Log and Concomitant Medication Log are mandatory for initial reports and for follow-up reports if any relevant changes have been made since the initial report.", "bboxes": [[72.00000000000011, 135.8639829101562, 541.0800000000002, 110.45497521784853]], "relevance": "medium"}, {"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 71, "section": "10.2 Electronic Case Record Form", "exactText": "Errors occurring in the e-CRF will be corrected electronically. Such corrections/modifications will be automatically tracked by an audit trail detailing the date and time of the correction and the name of the person making the 